 ## padding
 Inner padding around the text, in px.
 
+## inputType
+The native input type: `"text"` (default), `"password"`, `"email"`, `"tel"`, `"url"`,
+`"search"`, `"number"`. `"password"` is what hides what is typed **and** what a browser's
+password manager keys on; swap it to `"text"` reactively for a show-password control. Ignored
+on a `multiline` field.
+
+## autocomplete
+The HTML autofill token — `"email"`, `"username"`, `"current-password"`, `"cc-number"`,
+`"cc-exp"`, `"cc-csc"`, `"cc-name"`, `"address-line1"`, `"postal-code"`, …. Without it a
+browser's card, address and password autofill cannot tell the fields apart.
+
+## inputMode
+The on-screen keyboard to bring up: `"numeric"` for a card number or code, `"email"`,
+`"tel"`, `"decimal"`. A hint only — it constrains nothing; validate as usual.
+
+## fieldName
+The field's form name (HTML `name`) — a second signal autofill heuristics read beside
+`autocomplete`.
+
